DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzllooggiinn is the graphical front door of the hi-res machine.
     When ggeettttyy finds itself on the hi-res console (the console
     driver reports the vvtt110000 terminal type and the video card
     answers a memory probe), it replaces itself with zzllooggiinn
     instead of printing the textual login prompt.  zzllooggiinn paints
     a login panel directly on the bitmap display and reads the
     keyboard from the console in raw mode; no window server is
     running yet, and the mouse is not used.

     The panel holds a name field and a password field.  Print-
     able characters go to the field that holds the caret; the
     following keys edit and move:

          EEnntteerr           move from the name to the password field, or log in
          TTaabb             switch fields
          BBaacckkssppaaccee       erase the last character
          CCttrrll-UU          clear the field

     The password is shown as * characters.

     The name and password are checked against /eettcc/ppaasssswwdd by the
     same rules as llooggiinn: an account whose password field is
     empty needs no password.  As soon as the password is ac-
     cepted the panel is taken down and a LLaauunncchhiinngg zzvviieeww...
     notice is shown in its place until the desktop paints its
     first screen.  A successful login is recorded in /eettcc/uuttmmpp
     and /uussrr/aaddmm/wwttmmpp, the console is given to the user, the
     HHOOMMEE, PPAATTHH and TTEERRMM environment is set up, and zzllooggiinn
     replaces itself with /uussrr/hhrr/bbiinn/zzvviieeww, the desktop, running
     as the logged-in user.  When the desktop is quit, iinniitt
